From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:44:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: soc-core: leave trigger-muted DAIs muted on resume

The card resume unmutes every DAI with an active playback stream. A DAI
that sets mute_unmute_on_trigger is meant to be unmuted only while its
stream runs, but after system resume the stream is suspended, prepared
or paused, and a PCM without SNDRV_PCM_INFO_RESUME may not run again
until userspace prepares it, if ever.

Leave such DAIs muted at resume. The trigger unmutes them on RESUME or
START.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/soc-core.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/soc-core.c b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
index eb878528fd2c..2ee43f57c459 100644
--- a/sound/soc/soc-core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
@@ -483,8 +483,11 @@ static void soc_playback_digital_mute(struct snd_soc_card *card, int mute)
 			continue;
 
 		for_each_rtd_dais(rtd, i, dai) {
-			if (snd_soc_dai_stream_active(dai, playback))
-				snd_soc_dai_digital_mute(dai, mute, playback);
+			if (!snd_soc_dai_stream_active(dai, playback))
+				continue;
+			if (!mute && snd_soc_dai_mute_is_ctrled_at_trigger(dai))
+				continue;
+			snd_soc_dai_digital_mute(dai, mute, playback);
 		}
 	}
 }
